From: rosy-port <ace@localhost>
Date: Sat, 22 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 1007 rosy: FocalTech FT8006M touch screen on QUP3

rosy has a FocalTech FT8006M at 0x38 on BLSP1 QUP3 (i2c-3), reset GPIO64,
attn GPIO65 -- from the stock device tree.  vince_input.c already carries a
proven QUP3 FIFO I2C transport for this same SoC and the same QUP3 block;
rosy_touch.c reuses it and adds the vendor FT8006M register layout and the
report parser from research/ft8006 (the Xiaomi/LineageOS fts_ts driver).

The report is one flat buffer in which the register address equals the byte
offset, so the coordinate bytes of record 0 are read from register 3 (the
vendor driver's divided path reads them from 0x09 only because it already
read 9 bytes).  Reading them from register 4, or not at all for a single
finger, shifts every record by one byte and yields coordinates above the
panel size.

Polled on one kernel thread, no IRQ and no PMIC writes.  If the IC does not
answer, its supply is the likely cause (DTB: vdd = PMI8940 IBB 0xdc00,
lab = 0xde00) and the log says so rather than writing PMIC registers blind.
The first five contact frames are always dumped, and every 200 frames the
largest raw coordinates seen are printed, so one boot shows whether the IC
reports panel pixels (0..719 / 0..1439) or a 12-bit full scale.

Also fixes the ROSY touch geometry in SweetHID.cpp: the panel is 720x1440
portrait (VINCE_FB_W/H), not the transposed 1440x720, and drops the
SWEET_TOUCH_PANEL_W redefinition warning.

Boot-args: rosytouch=0 off, rosytouchdelay=N, rosytouchdump=1.

